  "reveal": {
    "ledger_voiced": "The whispered voice came by my art of the thrown voice, pitched low and hollow as the sitters wished to hear it. The cold draught was nothing but a trimmed wick, the lamp guttering when my knee found the leaf of the table. The touch—a stuffed glove, worn beneath my sleeve and produced at the moment of maximum darkness. The raps were silk thread, drawn across the underside when attention wandered upward. The scent of violets, a phial decanted into the air at the séance's crescendo. One effect I did not produce: the spirit trumpet rang out of my direction entirely, and I did not care to know its source.\n\nThe Reverend Simeon Gaunt came to the sitting with murder already decided. His hands left the circle long before the lights failed—long enough to do what required doing to Cousin R. That cousin was found past any sitting's reach, past any medium's particular art. The Reverend's account of the dark was an invention sewn as carefully as my own, but his threads were murderous and mine merely mercenary.\n\nThe dead, I have always held, say precisely what it profits them to say; on this evening, it profited the Reverend Gaunt far more than it profited me.",
